{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 accuracy. scvi_n200 + multiprofile is clearly the strongest RNA setup (0.650-0.653), and avgpool/transformer are nearly equivalent for this encoder. Image-only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208), suggesting limited standalone image signal. Uncertainty: We have not yet tested whether fusing image features—even weak ones—can provide complementary information beyond the RNA channel. This experiment tests multimodal fusion (weighted) with the best RNA encoder (scvi_n200), multiprofile, and avgpool aggregation. Weighted fusion is preferred over concat because it allows the model to down-weight the weaker image modality, reducing the risk of noise degradation. This is the best use of experiment 8 because it directly probes whether the current 0.653 ceiling can be broken by adding a second modality; if it succeeds, the remaining 2 experiments can refine fusion/aggregation; if it fails, we confirm RNA-only is optimal and can spend remaining budget on minor RNA-side variations (e.g., scgpt+multiprofile)."
}

